,\\,\\,-3x-6 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-3x-3}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nFrom the given polynomial division, we deduce that dividing the polynomial $5{x}^{2}+2x-6$ by the linear binomial $x+1$ gives\n\n- the quotient $5x-3,$ and\n\n- the remainder $-3.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{5{x}^{2}+2x-6}{x+1}=5x-3-\\frac{3}{x+1}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054087/state.json" "file_sha256" "51621fba6a71d097a49ff59c5aee2107677bf3bc1b4fc00f89571ef0457deb9b"} {"question" "q-113827" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054087/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "37f4fba8af6c9d082645aad0e8d48fb15b942519a42465a144f89be1051a5d0e"} {"question" "q-113827" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054087/state.json" "file_sha256" "51621fba6a71d097a49ff59c5aee2107677bf3bc1b4fc00f89571ef0457deb9b"} {"question" "q-113827" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "5x+3-\\frac{1}{x+1}"] ["math" "5x-1+\\frac{5}{x+1}"] ["math" "5x-2+\\frac{1}{x+1}"] ["math" "5x-3-\\frac{3}{x+1}"] ["math" "5x-5-\\frac{2}{x+1}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054087/state.json" "file_sha256" "51621fba6a71d097a49ff59c5aee2107677bf3bc1b4fc00f89571ef0457deb9b"} {"question" "q-113827" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5x-3-\\frac{3}{x+1}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054087/state.json" "file_sha256" "51621fba6a71d097a49ff59c5aee2107677bf3bc1b4fc00f89571ef0457deb9b"} {"question" "q-320860" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following polynomial division:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,3x+4 \\\\  & x-3\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,3{x}^{2}-5x-10\\,\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{3{x}^{2}-9x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,4x-10 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{4x-12}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the above, we conclude the following:\n\n| $3{x}^{2}-5x-10$ | $=$ | {{field-1}} | $+\\,\\,$ | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x-3$ |  | $x-3$ |  |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054087/state.json" "file_sha256" "51621fba6a71d097a49ff59c5aee2107677bf3bc1b4fc00f89571ef0457deb9b"} {"question" "q-320860" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,3x+4 \\\\  & x-3\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,3{x}^{2}-5x-10\\,\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{3{x}^{2}-9x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,4x-10 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{4x-12}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given polynomial division, we deduce that dividing the polynomial $3{x}^{2}-5x-10$ by the linear binomial $x-3$ gives\n\n- the quotient $3x+4,$ and\n\n- the remainder $2.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{3{x}^{2}-5x-10}{x-3}=3x+4+\\frac{2}{x-3}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054087/state.json" "file_sha256" "51621fba6a71d097a49ff59c5aee2107677bf3bc1b4fc00f89571ef0457deb9b"} {"question" "q-320860" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacade