\n\nFrom the above, $\\frac{{x}^{3}-1}{x-3}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054087/state.json" "file_sha256" "51621fba6a71d097a49ff59c5aee2107677bf3bc1b4fc00f89571ef0457deb9b"} {"question" "q-104218" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{x}^{2}+3x+9 \\\\  & x-3\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,{x}^{3}+0{x}^{2}+0x-1\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,3{x}^{2}+0x-1 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{3{x}^{2}-9x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,9x-1 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{9x-27}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,26\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given polynomial division, we deduce that dividing the polynomial ${x}^{3}-1$ by the linear binomial $x-3$ gives\n\n- the quotient ${x}^{2}+3x+9,$ and\n\n- the remainder $26.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{3}-1}{x-3}={x}^{2}+3x+9+\\frac{26}{x-3}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054087/state.json" "file_sha256" "51621fba6a71d097a49ff59c5aee2107677bf3bc1b4fc00f89571ef0457deb9b"} {"question" "q-104218" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054087/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "37f4fba8af6c9d082645aad0e8d48fb15b942519a42465a144f89be1051a5d0e"} {"question" "q-104218" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054087/state.json" "file_sha256" "51621fba6a71d097a49ff59c5aee2107677bf3bc1b4fc00f89571ef0457deb9b"} {"question" "q-104218" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "26+\\frac{x-3}{{x}^{2}+3x+9}"] ["math" "26+\\frac{{x}^{2}+3x+9}{x-3}"] ["math" "x-3+\\frac{26}{{x}^{2}+3x+9}"] ["math" "{x}^{2}+3x+9+\\frac{26}{x-3}"] ["math" "{x}^{3}-1+\\frac{26}{x-3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054087/state.json" "file_sha256" "51621fba6a71d097a49ff59c5aee2107677bf3bc1b4fc00f89571ef0457deb9b"} {"question" "q-104218" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{x}^{2}+3x+9+\\frac{26}{x-3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054087/state.json" "file_sha256" "51621fba6a71d097a49ff59c5aee2107677bf3bc1b4fc00f89571ef0457deb9b"} {"question" "q-37977" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "From top to bottom, what are the missing expressions in the following polynomial division problem?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\boxed{} \\\\  & x-1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,3{x}^{3}+0{x}^{2}+0x+5\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{3{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,3{x}^{2}+0x+5 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\boxed{}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,3x+5 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{3x-3}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,8\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054087/state.json" "file_sha256" "51621fba6a71d097a49ff59c5aee2107677bf3bc1b4fc00f89571ef0457deb9b"} {"question" "q-37977" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that the dividend is missing the ${x}^{2}$-term and the $x$-term. So, we write it using a zero coefficient, as follows:\n\n$$\n3{x}^{3}+0{x}^{2}+0x+5\n$$\n\nUsing the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,3{x}^{2}+3x+3 \\\\  & x-1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,3{x}^{3}+0{x}^{2}+0x+5\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{3{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,3{x}^{2}+0x+5 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{3{x}^{2}-3x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,3x+5 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{3x-3}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expressions are\n\n$\\,$ $3{x}^{2}+3x+3\\,$ and $\\,3{x}^{2}-3x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054087/state.json" "file_sha256" "51621fba6a71d097a49ff59c5aee2107677bf3bc1b4fc00f89571ef0457deb9b"} {"question" "q-37977" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054087/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "37f4fba8af6c9d082645aad0e8d48fb15b942519a42465a144f89be1051a5d0e"} {"question" "q-37977" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054087/state.json" "file_sha256" "51621fba6a71d097a49ff59c5aee2107677bf3bc1b4fc00f89571ef0457deb9b"} {"question" "q-37977" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$3{x}^{2}+3x+3\\,$ and $\\,3x-3$"] ["text" "$3{x}^{2}+3x+3\\,$ and $\\,3{x}^{2}-3x$"] ["text" "$3{x}^{2}+x-3\\,$ and $\\,3{x}^{2}-3x$"] ["text" "$3{x}^{2}-3x+1\\,$ and $\\,3x+3$"] ["text" "$3{x}^{2}-3x+3\\,$ and $\\,3{x}^{2}+3x$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054087/state.json" "file_sha256" "51621fba6a71d097a49ff59c5aee2107677bf3bc1b4fc00f89571ef0457deb9b"} {"question" "q-37977" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$3{x}^{2}+3x+3\\,$ and $\\,3{x}^{2}-3x$"] "category" "ma_successfu