\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2x+20 \\\\  & x-4\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,2{x}^{2}+12x+25\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{2{x}^{2}-\\,\\,8x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,20x+25 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{20x-80}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,105 \\\\  & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expressions are $2x+20$ and $20x+25.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054087/example-5032.json" "file_sha256" "323879b97a226ed51b10ab46084d064a3d7b29568098a8fe5cf545b7c085a386"} {"question" "e-5110" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following polynomial division:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2x-2 \\\\  & x+5\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,2{x}^{2}+8x-5\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{2{x}^{2}+10x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-2x-5 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-2x-10}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the above, what is $\\dfrac{2x^2+8x-5}{x+5}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054087/example-5110.json" "file_sha256" "aafcdfa24360d4e7f6704354c650ce1aff5b01b8900dfdd07481aa4db3f91a71"} {"question" "e-5110" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2x-2 \\\\  & x+5\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,2{x}^{2}+8x-5\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{2{x}^{2}+10x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-2x-5 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-2x-10}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given polynomial division, we deduce that dividing the polynomial $2x^2+8x -5$ by the linear binomial ${\\color{purple}x+5}$ gives\n\n- the quotient ${\\color{blue}2x-2},$ and\n\n- the remainder ${\\color{red}5}.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2x^2+8x-5}{x+5} = {\\color{blue}2x-2}+\\dfrac{\\color{red}5}{\\color{purple}x+5}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054087/example-5110.json" "file_sha256" "aafcdfa24360d4e7f6704354c650ce1aff5b01b8900dfdd07481aa4db3f91a71"} {"question" "e-5033" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "From top to bottom, what are the missing expressions in the following polynomial division problem?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\boxed{\\text{[math]\\phantom{x^2 - x + 1}[/math]}} \\\\  & x+1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,{x}^{3}+0{x}^{2}+0x+64\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-\\,{x}^{2}+0x+64 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,{x}^{2}-x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\boxed{\\text{[math]\\phantom{x + 64}[/math]}} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{x+1}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,63\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054087/example-5033.json" "file_sha256" "32dbf526d107cc369f7d1687c6e8b34dea9f918a05224113abcf8748642d1364"} {"question" "e-5033" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that the dividend is missing the $x^2$-term and the $x$-term. So, we write it using zero coefficients, as follows:\n\n$$\nx^3+{\\color{red}0}x^2 + {\\color{red}0}x + 64\n$$\n\nUsing the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{x}^{2}-x+1 \\\\  & x+1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,{x}^{3}+0{x}^{2}+0x+64\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-\\,{x}^{2}+0x+64 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,{x}^{2}-x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,x+64 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{x+1}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,63\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expressions are\n\n$\\qquad$ $x^2 - x + 1\\quad$ and $\\quad x + 64.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054087/example-5033.json" "file_sha256" "32dbf526d107cc369f7d1687c6e8b34dea9f918a05224113abcf8748642d1364"}] "usage" {"e-5033" [] "e-5032" [] "q-104126" [] "e-5110" [] "q-104226" [] "q-104218" []} "basis" 1796 "retractions" [[17592186129339 :question/problem "From top to bottom, what are the missing expressions in the following polynomial division problem?\n\n$2x + 2; 3x - 16x^{2} + 4x + 3; 6x^{2} - 2x_(―); 6x^{2} +6x + 3; 6x^{2} +6x - 2_(―); 6x^{2} + 4x +5$"] [17592186129342 :question/problem "Consider the following polynomial division:\n\n$x - 3x^{2} + 3x + 9; x - 3x^{3} + 0x^{2} + 0x - 01; x - 3x^{3} - 3x^{2}_(―); x - 3x^{3} -3x^{2} + 0x - 01; x - 3x^{3} -3x^{2} - 9x_(―); x - 3x^{3} - 0x^{2} +9x - 01; x - 3x^{3} - 0x^{2} +9x - 27_(―); x - 3x^{3} - 0x^{2} + 0x -26$\n\nFrom the above, $\\frac{x^{3} - 1}{x - 3} =$"] [17592186129343 :question/problem "From top to bottom, what are the missing expressions in the following polynomial division problem?\n\n$2x + 102x - 10; 2x + 104x^{2} + 00x - 005; 2x + 104x^{2} + 20x_(―); 2x + 104x^{2} - 20x - 005; 2x + 104x^{2}- 20x - 100_(―); 2x + 104x^{2} - 20x - 095$"] [17592186128867 :question/problem "From top to bottom, what are the missing expressions in the following polynomial division problem?\n\n$[math]\\phantom{2x+20}[/math]; x - 42x^{2} + 12x + 25; 2x^{2} - 8x_(―); 4x^{2} -[math]\\phantom{20x+25}[/math]; 4x^{2} -20x - 80_(―); 4x^{2} + 26x105$"] [17592186128867 :question/worked-solution "Using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n2x + 20; x - 42x^{2} + 12x + 25; 2x^{2} - 8x_(―); 4x^{2} -20x + 25; 4x^{2} -20x - 80_(―); 4x^{2} + 26x105\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expressions are $2x+20$ and $20x+25$."] [17592186128870 :question/problem "Consider the following polynomial division:\n$x + 22x - 2; x + 52x^{2} + 18x - 15; x + 22x^{2} + 10x- 15_(―); x + 23x^{2}- 12x - 15; x + 23x^{2}- 12x - 10_(―); x + 23x^{2} - 2x -15$\n\nFrom the above, what is $\\dfrac{2x^2+8x-5}{x+5}$?"] [17592186128870 :question/worked-solution "$$\nx + 22x - 2; x + 52x^{2} + 18x - 15; x + 22x^{2} + 10x- 15_(―); x + 23x^{2}- 12x - 15; x + 23x^{2}- 12x - 10_(―); x + 23x^{2} - 2x -15\n$$\n\nFrom the given polynomial division, we deduce that dividing the polynomial $2x^2+8x -5$ by the linear binomial ${\\color{purple}x+5}$ gives\n\n- the quotient ${\\color{blue}2x-2}$, and\n- the remainder ${\\color{red}5}$.\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2x^2+8x-5}{x+5} = {\\color{blue}2x-2}+\\dfrac{\\color{red}5}{\\color{purple}x+5}\n$$"] [17592186128868 :question/problem "From top to bottom, what are the missing expressions in the following polynomial division problem?\n\n$x + 1[math]\\phantom{x^2 - x + 1}[/math]; x + 1x^{3} + 0x^{2} + 0x + 64; x + 1x^{3} + 0x^{2}_(―); x + 1x^{3}- 0x^{2} + 0x + 64; x + 1x^{3}- 0x^{2} - 0x_(―); x + 1x^{3} - x^{2} -[math]\\phantom{x + 64}[/math]; x + 1x^{3} - x^{2} -x + 11_(―); x + 1x^{3} - x^{2} + x -63$"] [17592186128868 :question/worked-solution "Notice that the dividend is missing the $x^2$-term and the $x$-term. So, we write it using zero coefficients, as follows:\n\n$$\nx^3+{\\color{red}0}x^2 + {\\color{red}0}x + 64\n$$\n\nUsing the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$x + 1x^{2} - x + 1; x + 1x^{3} + 0x^{2} + 0x + 64; x + 1x^{3} + 0x^{2}_(―); x + 1x^{3}- 0x^{2} + 0x + 64; x + 1x^{3}- 0x^{2} - 0x_(―); x + 1x^{3} - x^{2} -x + 64; x + 1x^{3} - x^{2} -x + 11_(―); x + 1x^{3} - x^{2} + x -63$\nTherefore, the missing expressions are\n\n$\\qquad$ $x^2 - x + 1\\quad$ and $\\quad x + 64$."]] "immutable_answers" [17592186125841 17592186125842 17592186125843 17592186125844 17592186125845 17592186125859 17592186125860 17592186125861 17592186125862 17592186125863 17592186125865 17592186125866 17592186125867 17592186125868 17592186125869] "immutable_fields" [[1759218612584